title: v0.36.0 hardening pass — PNG export fixed, blocking .atelier corruption fixed, studio client extracted
summary: 'Team-driven quality pass on the v0.34/v0.35 surface, triggered by ''fix all things.'' Two review agents (reviewer Judge x2) + runtime smoke tests found real defects; six builders fixed them across 5 commits. Highlights: (1) PNG export was DEAD on fresh install — canvas was an optional peer dep needing brew install cairo pango; swapped to @napi-rs/canvas (prebuilt binaries) so export-image/carousel/still produce real PNGs out of the box (verified file out.png → PNG 1080x1080). (2) BLOCKING .atelier corruption: autosave loadFile never cleared the pending saveTimeout, so editing A then switching to B within 800ms wrote A''s bytes to B — fixed via a new SaveCoordinator (clear timer + flushPending to the correct file on switch). (3) /mcp WS endpoint was unreachable by real MCP clients (Origin check rejected missing-Origin) — split so /bridge stays strict, /mcp tolerates missing but rejects foreign. (4) Phantom agent-edit toast on every file open (system-source fell through broadcast filter). (5) Subfolder new-file + bridge persist ENOENT (no mkdir). (6) Slider drag flooded undo+bridge (split onInput preview vs onChange commit). (7) isSafePath over-broad. (8) import-images half-mutated doc (COW). (9) recipe new/validate path-resolution mismatch + double-extension. (10) Extracted the ~700-LOC inline studio client from a template-literal STRING into a typechecked module (packages/cli/src/web/inline-app.ts, bootStudioApp) with a dedicated DOM tsconfig — the root cause that let the save-race + slider bugs hide. Verified end-to-end: studio boots, scaffolds welcome.atelier, Vite transpiles the extracted module cleanly, POST save round-trips. Tests 676→696 passing, 0 skipped (was 3; PNG tests now run), 23/23 typechecks. Released v0.36.0.'
symbols_touched:
  - '#render-image'
