commit: c4a9bf5
learnings:
  - 'Reviewer agents earn their keep: a broad audit caught a BLOCKING .atelier-corruption autosave race that all the unit tests + typecheck missed (it only manifests on a timing-dependent fast file switch). Pair agent review with runtime smoke tests — my own export-image smoke test caught that PNG export was dead-on-arrival (optional canvas peer dep) which no test covered because the tests were skipped for the same reason. The inline studio app being a template-literal STRING was the meta-bug: ~700 LOC of WS/bridge/autosave logic invisible to tsc/lint/tests'
  - which is exactly where the two worst bugs lived; extracting it to a typechecked module (bootStudioApp + a 2-line entry shim + a DOM-scoped tsconfig so client/server lib types don't clash) is the durable fix. ALWAYS verify a studio-client refactor by booting the server + curling the Vite-transpiled module + a save round-trip — tsc cannot see template-string client code
  - and now can.
